From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zerollama <zerollama@local>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 17:16:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ollama: multi-GPU SWA flash-attn, mmproj VRAM, prompt truncation

Fix remaining dual-GPU gemma4 / SWA / vision crashes in llama.cpp so Go
no longer needs --flash-attn off, --ctx-checkpoints 0, or -ts 1,1 band-aids.

- fit: track n_swa; prefer equal full-layer split for multi-GPU SWA; skip
  partial-layer overflow that breaks dual KV caches
- llama-context: re-probe FA/KV device placement when flash-attn is forced
  on multi-GPU (not only when auto)
- server: disable mmproj GPU offload when no device has projector + 1 GiB free
- server: truncate oversized prompts at launch (media-chunk aware)

Tested: gemma4:26b-a4b-it-qat + mmproj, 2x RTX 4090, ~7.1k token prefill,
--flash-attn auto, --ctx-checkpoints 32, no -ts, no CUDA errors.

